17592186420710 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420710 1083 #uuid "7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420711 1080 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420711 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420711 1083 #uuid "7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420707 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420708 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420709 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420710 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420711 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1077 "selection" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420707 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420712 1079 #uuid "f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420712 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1069 "q-35759" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1071 "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1072 #uuid "0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420713 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -5{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4{x}_{2} \\\\ 20{x}_{2} & -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 20 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -12 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 15 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are  the $1$st,  $2$nd and $3$rd. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B,C}$ is linearly independent." 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420714 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420715 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420714 1062 #uuid "13861d32-2afe-51b5-bbef-cdba909877c7" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420714 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360491 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420715 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420717 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420715 1062 #uuid "26514834-a2cf-541c-940e-f1a92276ce78" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420715 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244004 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420716 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420714 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420716 1062 #uuid "91898925-eff3-5fa3-8a62-f041326f9f41" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420716 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420713 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420717 1062 #uuid "9a3eaaac-6a96-5a5c-a458-0780e627e72a" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420717 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244008 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420718 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420716 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420718 1062 #uuid "a04781cc-ebc3-5bc2-92d1-20e2247f29f6" 13194139534416 17592186045417 true] [17592186420718 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415061 13194139534416 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-86f80e75-0963-5bd9-910a-02c8b66996e2" 17592186420706 "answer-19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" 17592186420707 "answer-37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" 17592186420708 "answer-561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" 17592186420709 "answer-7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" 17592186420710 "answer-7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" 17592186420711 "answer-field-f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" 1